; minishop.claims — the questions, kept beside the model.
;
; Read by `writ check --claims`, and by `writ query` as a sibling file named
; after the model (so this must sit next to the generated minishop.writ).
;
; ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS. `check` lists, for each law, the moves that write a fact
; the law reads — whether or not they break it today. Accepting one says "I
; know this move touches this law, and I have thought about it." Two findings
; fall out of that, and both cost exit 1:
;
;   undeclared — a move that can break a law and was never accepted. Usually
;                a move you just added, or a law you just widened.
;   stale      — a move accepted against a law it cannot touch. Usually a law
;                that was narrowed and an acknowledgement nobody removed.
;
; This is drift detection for the model's own edit history, and it is why the
; acknowledgements are worth keeping in the repository rather than passing
; --strict and moving on.

(accept store-fails-saturated datastore-health-matches-state)
(accept store-fails-stopped   datastore-health-matches-state)

(accept api-fails-down                    service-health-matches-state)
(accept store-saturated-triggers-api-down service-health-matches-state)
(accept store-stopped-triggers-api-down   service-health-matches-state)

; Which stores have an exhausted connection pool, in whichever situation the
; query is asked at. `writ query minishop.writ saturated-stores --at 2`.
(query saturated-stores
  (where (s datastore))
  (and (is s.available yes)
       (is s.connection-count at-or-above-500)))
